{'symbol': 'UAL', 'date': '2020-05-22 20:30:00', 'title': 'UNITED AIRLINES TO PAY CEO SCOTT KIRBY AN ANNUAL BASE SALARY OF $1 MLN', 'text': 'UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED AN ANNUAL COMPENSATION PACKAGE FOR SCOTT KIRBY WITH AN ANNUAL BASE SALARY OF $1 MILLION.UNITED AIRLINES - TARGET ANNUAL INCENTIVE PROGRAM OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO 250% OF BASE SALARY FOR SCOTT KIRBY WAS APPROVED.UNITED AIRLINES - TARGET LONG-TERM INCENTIVE (“LTI”) OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO TEN TIMES BASE SALARY FOR SCOTT KIRBY WAS APPROVED.UNITED AIRLINES - FOR PRESIDENT BRETT HART, COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED ANNUAL BASE SALARY OF $775,000.UNITED AIRLINES - FOR HART, APPROVED TARGET AIP OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO 175% OF BASE SALARY.UNITED AIRLINES - FOR HART, APPROVED TARGET LTI OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO 7.5 TIMES BASE SALARY.UNITED AIRLINES - BASED ON NEW COMPENSATION LEVELS, COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED, GRANTED LTI AWARDS OF $2.3 MILLION FOR KIRBY, $1.8 MILLION FOR HART.UNITED AIRLINES -  MAY 2020 LTI AWARDS FOR CEO SCOTT KIRBY AND PRESIDENT BRETT HART ARE IN FORM OF TIME-VESTED RESTRICTED STOCK UNITS.UNITED AIRLINES - NEW BASE SALARY, TOTAL COMPENSATION LEVELS APPROVED FOR SCOTT KIRBY AS CEO ARE LOWER THAN LEVELS FOR PRIOR CEO OSCAR MUNOZ.UNITED AIRLINES - ACKNOWLEDGES THAT DUE TO PSP AGREEMENT LIMITATIONS, KIRBY & HART MAY NOT REALIZE FULL VALUE OF RESPECTIVE COMPENSATION PACKAGES.UNITED AIRLINES - BASE SALARY, TOTAL COMPENSATION LEVELS APPROVED FOR HART AS PRESIDENT ARE LOWER THAN LEVELS FOR KIRBY IN HIS ROLE OF PRESIDENT.'}